title: "Hyper-Ramanujan (HR) Closed-Form Radical Approximations for 2D Ellipse Circumference and 3D Triaxial Ellipsoid Surface Area"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
url: "https://github.com/CodiBasti/HyperRamanujan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CodiBasti/HyperRamanujan"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ellipse circumference
  - ellipse perimeter
  - triaxial ellipsoid surface area
  - Ramanujan approximation
  - Hyper-Ramanujan
  - continued fractions
  - Pade approximants
  - complete elliptic integral
  - Carlson symmetric integral
  - special functions
abstract: >-
  Resolves the fourth-order accuracy mechanism of Ramanujan's 1914 second ellipse
  perimeter approximation via exact Stieltjes continued fraction periodicity (a3 = a4 = 3/16)
  and derives the exact reciprocal expansion of the inner-radical defect
  27*h^4 / delta(h) = 6144 - 7040*h + (5144/3)*h^2 - (413/9)*h^3 - (1081/108)*h^4 + O(h^5).
  Introduces five single-radical 2D Hyper-Ramanujan approximations (HR-7-Int, HR-6B, HR-8B,
  HR-8P, HR-6M) reaching full float64 precision at moderate eccentricities and 0.63 ppm
  (HR-8P) / 0.30 ppm (HR-6M) globally across h in [0, 1], as well as the 3D triaxial
  ellipsoid surface area generalization (HR-3D-10P) achieving < 16.8 ppm across all triaxial
  shapes using only one square root and zero fractional powers.
